# Nukkad Network

- project = Nukkad Network
- stack = Next.js App Router + TS + Tailwind, Supabase, EasySocial WhatsApp BSP, MSG91 OTP, Vercel cron, Recharts

## CORE RULES

- One active code per customer; a new scan supersedes the previous active code.
- Code format `NK-XXXXX`: uppercase alphanumeric, excluding `0`, `O`, `1`, `I`. Expiry is 7 days.
- Lifetime one redemption per customer per business.
- A code is invalid at its source business.
- Discount is 10% of gross, capped by the category rate card.
- Referrer earns 5% of GROSS and the platform earns 5% of GROSS, unless that category's rate card sets a flat amount.
- The next code is auto-issued and linked by `source_redemption_id`.
- Sunday settle, Monday block; marking a settlement paid unblocks the business.
- WhatsApp is a channel only. Postgres is the source of truth.
- The shopkeeper never generates codes.
- All database writes go through `SECURITY DEFINER` RPCs only.

## RATE CARDS

| Category | Discount | Cap | Referrer | Platform | Min bill |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Cafe | 10% | 80 | 5% gross | 5% gross | 0 |
| Salon | 10% | 200 | 5% gross | 5% gross | 0 |
| Laundry | 10% | 60 | 5% gross | 5% gross | 0 |
| Gym | 10% | 150 | 5% gross | 5% gross | 0 |
| Xerox | 10% | 20 | flat 5 | flat 5 | 50 |

## TABLES

`categories`, `rate_cards`, `businesses`, `customers`, `otp_codes`, `referral_codes`, `redemptions`, `commission_ledger`, `disputes`, `settlements`, `followup_responses`

